    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with a potent lineup anchored by **Kyle Tucker** (75.13) and **Jacob Wilson** (72.17), our strongest plays of the day. **Kyle Tucker** benefits from a highly favorable matchup against Brandon Pfaadt, who yields a 4.54 xERA, allowing **Kyle Tucker** to capitalize on the park factors and SP vulnerability. Meanwhile, **Jacob Wilson** faces Bennett and leverages a strong platoon edge and park environment to elevate his output. Both **Andy Pages** (72.12) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (68.96) also grade out as elite starts; **Andy Pages** is particularly well-positioned given the slow delivery of Brandon Pfaadt, which provides an opportunistic boost for his stolen base potential, while **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** benefits from favorable wind conditions and a solid spot in the order.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the lineup was navigating the outfield depth, with **Wade Meckler** (54.58) narrowly edging out **Sam Antonacci** (43.60) for the final spot. While **Sam Antonacci** saw a solid projection, his matchup against Gavin Williams\u2014an elite arm with a 2.91 xERA\u2014suppressed his efficiency score, pushing the optimizer toward **Wade Meckler**, who faces the more favorable Sandy Alcantara. We must remain cautious with **Gunnar Henderson** and **Heliot Ramos**, both of whom face high-tier pitching in Jacob deGrom and Chris Sale, respectively. Despite these difficult matchups, **Gunnar Henderson** remains a must-start due to his volume and dynamic platoon upside, though his score reflects the inherent risk of facing an elite arm.\n\nManagers should note that several slots are currently based on \"Lineup Pending\" assumptions, including **Liam Hicks**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Gunnar Henderson**, **Jorge Polanco**, **Andy Pages**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, and **Jackson Merrill**. If final lineups deviate significantly from these spots, particularly for **Jorge Polanco**\u2014who is already skating on the edge of our marginal start threshold\u2014adjustments will be necessary. We are prioritizing speed and matchup efficiency today, specifically monitoring **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jackson Merrill**, as their ability to exploit slow opposing pitchers creates a distinct advantage in our pursuit of stolen bases.",
